## Getting Started

These instructions will get a copy of this project running on your machine for development and testing purposes.

## Prerequisites

This project requires [Crystal](https://crystal-lang.org/) ([installation guide](https://crystal-lang.org/docs/installation/)).

## Development

<% if @project_type == "cli" -%>
To develop your CLI application:

1. Install dependencies with `shards install`
2. Build your application with `shards build`
3. Run your CLI with `./bin/<%= @project.downcase.gsub(/[^a-z0-9_]/, "_") %> --help`

## Usage

```bash
./bin/<%= @project.downcase.gsub(/[^a-z0-9_]/, "_") %> --help
```
<% else -%>
To start your Azu server:

1. Install dependencies with `shards install`
2. Check `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.development` (a SQLite file needs no server)
3. Create and migrate your database with `azu db:setup`
4. Start the development server with `azu serve`

Now you can visit http://localhost:<%= port %>/ from your browser.

In development the server listens on `127.0.0.1` only (azu's default; `.env` does not set `HOST`). To reach it from
another machine or from inside a container, set `HOST=0.0.0.0` in the environment (a real environment variable wins
over `.env`); other environments listen on `0.0.0.0` by default.

## Configuration

- **Database**: Configure your database connection in `src/initializers/cql_config.cr`
- **Server**: Adjust server settings in `src/server.cr`
- **Environment**: Use environment variables for configuration

## Database

This project uses [CQL](https://github.com/azutoolkit/cql) as the ORM. Database operations:

```bash
azu db create    # Create the database
azu db migrate   # Run migrations
azu db seed      # Seed with data
azu db reset     # Reset database
```
<% end -%>

## Tests

To run the test suite:

```bash
<% if @test_framework == "spec" -%>
crystal spec
<% else -%>
crystal run spec/test_helper.cr
<% end -%>
```

<% if @docker_support -%>
## Docker

The `Dockerfile` builds a release binary and runs it as a non-root user in production mode
(`CRYSTAL_ENV=production`), listening on `HOST` (`0.0.0.0` in the image) and `PORT` (<%= port %>). To run the app
in development inside a container, pass `-e HOST=0.0.0.0` (azu's development default `127.0.0.1` is unreachable from the host). The secrets are not in the image: pass them in.

```bash
docker build -t <%= @project %> .
docker run -p <%= port %>:<%= port %> -e CSRF_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32) -e SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32) <%= @project %>
```

Without `CSRF_SECRET` the container exits with `CSRF_SECRET is not set`. `SESSION_SECRET` is only needed once you
generate authentication (`azu generate auth`).
<% if database_adapter == "sqlite3" -%>
The SQLite database is `/data/<%= @project %>.db` on the `/data` volume (`-v <%= @project %>_data:/data`); the image does not run
migrations, so run `azu db:migrate` against that file first.
<% else -%>
Point `DATABASE_URL` at your database server (`-e DATABASE_URL=...`).
<% end -%>
<% end -%>

